From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rune Lillesveen <futhark@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 02:28:35 -0700
Subject: Disallow percentage in calc() for <length>

We should not allow values such as calc(4px * sign(10%)) as a valid
<length>.

Adjusted test_invalid_length() tests lacking a calc() wrapper which
made them incorrectly pass without the changes here.

This CL also disallows percentage in <length> for these cases:

calc(4px * sign(10% / 10%)
calc(4px * (10% / 10%))

There are open issues against the spec:

https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14300
https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12204
https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10017

The two latter aligns with the current Firefox Nightly.

It should be noted that we already disallowed percentages for other
value types such as <angle> and <resolution>.

Fixes a UAF issue where CalcHandles() are accessed from multiple
threads computing length values in a canvas worker thread.

Turn DCHECK() into CHECK() for IsMainThread() to crash instead of
doing cross thread access to CalcHandles().

Bug: 416644951, 567611695
Change-Id: I1e4be23733b3139d16986e3848323a99248f72f1
